  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="265" ed="#liebermann"/>And sawlsceat is rihtast, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man symle gelæste a æt openu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="13" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="122" ed="#robertson"/>And sawlsceat is rihtast þæt man symle gelæste a æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="194" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And sawlsceat is rihtast, þæt man symle gelæste a æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="265" ed="#liebermann"/>Und Seelengeld ist am richtigsten, dass man immer entrichte gleich bei noch offenem Grabe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And as for soul-scot, it is most right that it always be paid at once at the open grave.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIIIAtr_13.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="123" ed="#robertson"/>And it is best that payment for the souls of the dead should always be rendered before the grave is closed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="195" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And it is most appropriate that dues for the souls of the dead always be paid while the grave is yet open.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="265"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_20">VI Atr 20</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 20</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><ref target="clause:ICn_13">I Cn 13</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="24"><ref target="clause:ICn_13">I Cn 13–13.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 20.</note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIIIAtr_13.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">340</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 12; VI, 20.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
